    {
      "id": "2FDGcwmq",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1767.2001555047195,
      "y": -451.3463702923892,
      "width": 483.7278137207031,
      "height": 1155,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "dotted",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0H",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1692465278,
      "version": 898,
      "versionNonce": 1846612139,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1761716546566,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "        ------- Backlogs ----------\n\n1. Should we use generated\npydantic schema through LLM or\npredefined pydantic schema.\n\n2. How should we process the\nextracted data if the data subpar\nand has to go through HITL\n    - what will be the format of\nthe HITL review .\n    - what will be the next step\nafter a human provide its review .\n    - \n\n3. How do we calculate the data\nextraction quality ? what will be\nthe logic ?\n\n4. Evaluation Part can be done on\na manually-labelled dataset\ngenerated using synthesis.\n\n5. Still don't know how to calculate\nthe confidence score\n\n6. Still don't know how to decide if\nan image input is too complicated\n\n7. We might need a Regex\nGenerator - as a tool maybe.\n\n8. ",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "THxBR4Hd4OlchAp_kGN_2",
      "originalText": "        ------- Backlogs ----------\n\n1. Should we use generated pydantic schema through LLM or predefined pydantic schema.\n\n2. How should we process the extracted data if the data subpar and has to go through HITL\n    - what will be the format of the HITL review .\n    - what will be the next step after a human provide its review .\n    - \n\n3. How do we calculate the data extraction quality ? what will be the logic ?\n\n4. Evaluation Part can be done on a manually-labelled dataset generated using synthesis.\n\n5. Still don't know how to calculate the confidence score\n\n6. Still don't know how to decide if an image input is too complicated\n\n7. We might need a Regex Generator - as a tool maybe.\n\n8. ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
